      "text": [
        "**Latvian** belongs to the Baltic languages. The other major member of this branch is Lithuanian, to which it is closely related.",
        "Within the Baltic languages, the following letters are unique to Latvian:",
        "- Vowels with a macron (horizontal stripe): Ā Ē Ī.",
        "- Consonants with a small hook: Ģ Ķ Ļ Ņ.",
        "NOTE: Estonian is not a member of the Baltic languages(despite the name), and therefore looks significantly different."
      ],
      "tags": [],
      "images": [
        {
          "id": "b56743621134",
          "src": "https://www.plonkit.net/images/latvia/Latvian_language.png"
        }
      ],
      "locations": [],
      "lookalikes": [],
      "credit": {
        "source": "Plonk It",
        "url": "https://www.plonkit.net/latvia",
        "licence": "CC BY-NC-SA 4.0"
      },
      "summary": "Look for vowels with a bar on top (Ā Ē Ī) and consonants with a small hook (Ģ Ķ Ļ Ņ). Lithuanian is related; Estonian looks quite different.",
      "differs": [
        {
          "country": "LT",
          "how": "Related language but lacks these exact letters"
        },
        {
          "country": "EE",
          "how": "Not a Baltic language, looks very different"
        }
      ]
